  "verbalization": "Capsianoside Ii is consistently linked to SNU1 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Capsianoside Ii acts as a target for H9, which in turn is a target of both (+)-Narwedine and Calanolide D, all of which ultimately target SNU1. This indicates a potential pathway where Capsianoside Ii influences H9, which then modulates the activity of other compounds that target SNU1. The presence of multiple targets and their shared downstream effect on SNU1 suggests a possible mechanism involving the regulation of H9, which could modulate the activity of SNU1 through a complex network of interactions. The consistent scores across the three paths further support the reliability of this relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction between Capsianoside Ii and H9 remains to be fully elucidated.",
